  production in awe and i just remember  this harsh descending  over everyone the crown had help from  diana's wedding dress designers david  and elizabeth emanuel to make this  moment as realistic as possible overall  emma says during the process she got to  know diana like you would a friend  doctor  this is diana preparing for her role as  diana in the movie diana was no joke for  naomi watts before even starting  production she was put through a  three-month workout and diet regime in  order to get her frame as similar to  diana's as possible as for the emotional  part of it all naomi realized how  tedious it was to play someone like  diana i mean it's it's delicate however  she did all the research she could on  diana before diving into the role i read  all the biographies um i looked at every  piece of footage but she wanted to make  sure she didn't fall into trying to  mimic her she prepared so much there  were times she would even dream of diana  on set naomi spent hours in the makeup  chair having a prosthetic nose and  multiple wigs applied for the wardrobe  they were able to work with designer  jaka zoguri who created many of diana's  iconic pieces i created replicas of  dresses i had designed for princess  diana with an actress and team as good  as this one it's no wonder naomi was  able to give the world a very accurate  representation of the late princess this  is my princess diane  right from the start bonnie soper was  dedicated to making sure she did diana  justice the casting agents were shocked  when her audition included hair makeup  and costume inspired by the princess  however just their similarity and  appearance alone may have done the trick  her audition tape is just uncanny i like  to be a queen of people's hearts in  people's hearts bonnie says she did the  research for the role and was surprised  at how much her own instincts helped i  get sort of instinctive about some  things and i felt really positive about  this  although the productions she was a part  of weren't as widespread as some of the  other actresses her dedication to the  role did the princess justice it was no  secret that genevieve o'reilly wasn't  the most similar in appearance to  princess diana however she was able to  make up for it with her impeccable  preparation she trained herself with  voice and body language classes in order  to portray her near perfectly genevieve  doesn't look like diana but she can act  i'd think i was watching archive footage  of diana herself  genevieve was also given advice from an  unsuspected person while filming  genevieve was approached by a former  royal servant who told her keep your  chin down and your left eye slightly up  if you want to capture what she really  looked like sometimes it isn't hollywood  professionals who can give you the best  advice but those with real experience  you have to tell your story  i've had to sell mine julie cox fell  into playing diana in a whirlwind she  was cast just a few days before the  filming of princess in love began and  had never read a book or watched a  program about diana while there was the  obvious struggle of her having no  background history on the princess i  thought if i had read it i'll have a  hard time taking the script seriously  transforming her physically was also a  challenge not only did she have brown  hair which they did die but julie is  only five foot four inches in height  that's a whole six inches shorter than  diana was the environment on set was a  very difficult one for julie and the  crew who often complained about unfit  working conditions however in the end  they were able to pull it together and  get the film released  these are for you lovely thank you  serena scott thomas earned the title of  being one of the most identical diana's  that television had ever seen in diana  her true story with a wig and a costume  department that were able to match some  of diana's wardrobe pieces perfectly her  transformation was seamless some  reviewers even admitted to forgetting  they were watching an actress and not  diana herself  catherine oxenburg's portrayal of diana  in the royal romance of charles and  diana was very meta she's third cousins  with prince william and prince harry and  actually attended the ball the day  before diana's wedding something she  thinks makes her even more qualified for  the role at the ball right before their  wedding charles came up to me and he  said would you like to meet diana her  parents had been worried about how their  family would react to the film but  catherine felt she could do the princess  justice to prepare she says she took  many visits to buckingham palace  caroline bliss was one of the original  actors to ever tackle playing diana she  had the advantage of diana still being  alive and being present when the world  fell in love with diana experiencing it  firsthand do you think you'll ever be  queen  no i don't diana led a life of love  compassion and leadership that the world  will never forget while no actress may  ever come close to playing her perfectly  keeping her on the big screen in any  form is a gift to the world which  actress do you think portrayed diana the  best  [Music]
 

